    This command allows you to test a file for download before you actually
    download the file.  The testing procedure is determined by the SysOp so
    it may vary from system to system.
@X0F
   Subcommand
@X03
      @X0B(filename)      Filename to test. @X03 This is the file that will be tested
                      according to the testing procedures designated by the
                      SysOp. You may only specify one filename at a time.
@X0F
   Description
@X03
      How many times have you downloaded a file only to find that it will not
      uncompress due to errors?  The TEST command permits you to check files
      for viruses and other corruptions that might exist in a particular
      file.  When you enter the filename to test, you will be informed after
      a short delay whether the file passed or  failed the predetermined
      criteria.  If the filename you enter to test does not exist on the
      system, you will be notified that the filename you entered does not
      exist and you will be allowed to enter a new filename to test.
@XFF
